## the size record, written to <scratch>/w first
    # Size, Milestone 2 part 4a: 2026-09-29-3e67745
    
    The stripped `i686-unknown-linux-musl` sizes of the seventeen size probes,
    measured by `records/logs/m2p4a-p4/size.log` after Milestone 2 part 4a,
    names, links, properties and protection
    (`specs/0019-names-links-properties-protection.md`, "Size", under decision
    1 taken as A). The part's four capabilities are behind the Cargo feature
    `metadata`, off by default and outside the core; its cost is measured by
    `probe-emend-metadata-write-xml` beside the core probe. The budget is the
    core probe, `probe-emend-format-write-xml`, over `probe-zip-xml`, against
    the Milestone 2 ceiling (`specs/0017-fuller-styles.md`, decision 1, A),
    which this part does not move by design. This record follows
    `records/size-m2p3-2026-09-27-b728fdf.md`, part 3's, which stands as history.
    
    - Commit: 3e67745011d5a8e02a32de065175d3d0df3eb640
    - Date: 2026-09-29 (UTC)
    - Toolchain: rustc 1.98.1 (48a229cea 2026-09-01); cargo 1.98.1 (797e8a9bc 2026-08-05)
    - Target: i686-unknown-linux-musl
    - Profile: `size` in the workspace `Cargo.toml` (inherits release,
      opt-level "z", lto "fat", codegen-units 1, panic "abort", strip true,
      debug false)
    - `zip` 8.6.0, `default-features = false`, features
      `deflate-flate2-zlib-rs`; `quick-xml` 0.42.0 behind the `size-probe`
      feature `xml`; emend behind the `size-probe` feature `emend`; emend's
      `dates`, `rowcol` and `metadata` behind the `size-probe` features of
      the same names (`["emend", "xml", "emend/<feature>"]`)
    - Each probe built alone with its own `--features` set, the manifest's
      `required-features`; the core probes and `probe-emend-format-write-xml`
      with `emend,xml`, which turns on neither `rowcol` nor `metadata` (the
      log reads it off `cargo tree -e features`)
    
    ## The probes
    
    | Binary | What it does | File bytes | Section bytes | .text bytes |
    | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
    | `probe-zip` | opens an archive with `zip`, prints the entry count | 473636 | 464320 | 364751 |
    | `probe-zip-xml` | the same, then reads one entry through `zip` and counts its elements with `quick-xml` | 539172 | 533216 | 411155 |
    | `probe-zip-xml-write` | `probe-zip-xml`, then writes one deflated entry to a second archive through the `zip` crate's `ZipWriter` | 612900 | 606004 | 461107 |
    | `probe-emend-copy` | opens an archive with emend and writes it back with no edits | 584228 | 579588 | 441139 |
    | `probe-emend-edit` | opens with emend, reads the entry to replace, and writes a replace, a removal and an addition from its command line | 649764 | 641964 | 489395 |
    | `probe-emend-edit-xml` | `probe-emend-edit`, plus the `quick-xml` element count over the replaced entry's bytes | 666148 | 658124 | 502291 |
    | `probe-emend-package-xml` | opens with `Package`, resolves the workbook, drops the calculation chain, adds an override and a `theme` relationship, replaces a part through `Stream`, writes the package, counts the replaced part's elements | 858660 | 852012 | 667827 |
    | `probe-emend-cells-xml` | `probe-emend-package-xml`, plus the shared strings and every cell of the named sheet: the cell count, the sum of `number()` and the length of the `resolve`d text | 903716 | 896884 | 697363 |
    | `probe-emend-cells-write-xml` | `probe-emend-cells-xml`, then on the named sheet `set_cell` of a number, a text and a boolean and `clear_cell` of a fourth reference, `drop_calc_chain`, the write to a second path, and that sheet's cell count read back through `Package::cells` | 907812 | 900832 | 700675 |
    | `probe-emend-styles-write-xml` | `probe-emend-cells-write-xml`, then on the same package `styles()` counts, `add_cell_style` on base 0 with a `Code` from its command line and on base none with `BuiltIn(14)`, `set_cell_style` of the first on the number cell and the second on the text cell; after the write the output's `styles()` counts and the two cells' `style` through `Package::cells` | 928292 | 921804 | 718115 |
    | `probe-emend-dates-write-xml` | `probe-emend-styles-write-xml` with the `dates` feature: the number cell holds the serial of a `DateTime` from its command line in the epoch `Epoch::of` reads, and `from_serial` of the number read back is printed | 932388 | 926628 | 722499 |
    | `probe-emend-formulas-write-xml` | `probe-emend-styles-write-xml`, then `set_cell` of a `Formula` from its command line on a third cell, so the write's formula-change rule runs and the workbook part's `calcPr` is rewritten; after the write the output's `Workbook::full_calc_on_load` and `calc_chain`, and the third cell's `formula` through `Package::cells` | 928292 | 922996 | 719043 |
    | `probe-emend-sheets-write-xml` | `probe-emend-formulas-write-xml`, then on the same package before its write `add_sheet` of a name from its command line, `move_sheet` of it to 0, `rename_sheet` of it, `remove_sheet` of the sheet that was first; after the write the output's sheet count and the first sheet's name and part lengths; and `Package::new()` written to a third path with its byte count | 969252 | 962076 | 748051 |
